{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.rho_trM_radial_ansatz_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.rho_trM_radial_ansatz_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**Capstone.** The `ρ = tr_M` radial ansatz (with `Vol(T)=Vol(³He)`) is refuted: the C_knot and\ntr_M mirror ratios lie on opposite sides of 1 (`mirror_test_excludes_rho_trM`). scope-(a): the radial\nhandle survives only with `ρ ≠ tr_M` or `Vol(T) ≠ Vol(³He)`; nothing wired, no fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.mirror_test_excludes_rho_trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.mirror_test_excludes_rho_trM","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.lean#L50-L63","doc":"**Mirror test refutes `ρ = tr_M` under equal Vol.** Assume the radial ansatz with a common volume:\n`C_knot(T) = Vol·tr_M(T)/ℏ_q²` and `C_knot(³He) = Vol·tr_M(³He)/ℏ_q²` at the witnessed values. Then the\nratio identity forces `C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) = tr_M(T)/tr_M(³He)`, but the former is `> 1` and the\nlatter `< 1` — contradiction. Hence no common `Vol, ℏ_q²` reproduce `C_knot` from `ρ = tr_M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.trM_ratio_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.trM_ratio_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.cknot_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.cknot_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.lean#L44-L46","doc":"**The witnessed ratios straddle unity.** `C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) > 1` (T more bound) while the\nper-block density ratio `ρ(T)/ρ(³He) = tr_M(T)/tr_M(³He) < 1` (T smaller trace). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.mirror_ratio_of_radial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.mirror_ratio_of_radial","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.lean#L34-L42","doc":"**The radial ansatz forces the mirror ratio identity.** If `C_knot(K) = Vol·ρ(K)/h` with a COMMON\nvolume `Vol` and `h = ℏ_q²` (the shared geometric dressing), then `C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) = ρ(T)/ρ(³He)`\n— Vol and h cancel. (Generic field algebra; `V, h, rHe ≠ 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}